A command whose a.go, b.go and c.go each write a directive that a line directive
renders at main.go:19:1, above alpha, bravo and charlie. Alpha is dead, so its
directive is in effect; bravo and charlie are called, so each of their directives
is stale, and each is reported where it renders.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- a.go --
package main

//line main.go:19:1
//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- kept for the loader
func alpha() {}
-- b.go --
package main

//line main.go:19:1
//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- kept for the loader
func bravo() {}
-- c.go --
package main

//line main.go:19:1
//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- kept for the loader
func charlie() {}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {
	bravo()
	charlie()
}
